<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shantala Devi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1131</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Shantala</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shantala Devi was the queen of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hoysala-empire">Hoysala</a> king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vishnuvardhana">Vishnuvardhana</a>, celebrated in inscriptions as an accomplished dancer and musician. A devout Jain, she endowed Jain shrines at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shravanabelagola">Shravanabelagola</a>, while her husband patronised Vaishnava temples. Tradition links her to the dancing figures of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belur">Belur</a> temple.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shantala-devi.jpg" alt="Shantala Devi" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Utpal Basu · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SHANTALA_DEVI_-_panoramio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
